The Approach I used:- 
1. Basically when I read the line "Without using standard Sort STL function" then I thought to use a data structure in STL which automatically sorts the numbers upon inserting in it randomly.

2.First I used ordered Set there it will remove duplicates so I used Multi set here duplicates are also inserted but everything in sorted order

3.storing in MultiSet and then modify each element of the array is the approach I used.

Code i used:- 

class Solution {
public:
    void sortColors(vector<int>& nums) {
        multiset<int> s;
        
        for(int i = 0 ; i< nums.size();i++){
            s.insert(nums[i]);
        }
        int j = 0;
        for(auto it: s){
            nums[j] = it;
            j++;
        }
    }
};